<group prefix="WebGpuSharp.FFI.">
    <comment location="WebGPU_FFI">
        <summary>            
            WebGPU FFI (Foreign Function Interface) functions.
            This is a low-level interface to the WebGPU API, allowing for direct access to the underlying C API.
        </summary>
    </comment>
    <group prefix="WebGPU_FFI.">
        <comment location="ARRAY_LAYER_COUNT_UNDEFINED">
            <summary>                
                The const value use to indicate that
            <see cref="WebGpuSharp.FFI.TextureViewDescriptorFFI.ArrayLayerCount">ArrayLayerCount</see>                
                is undefined.
            </summary>
        </comment>
        <comment location="COPY_STRIDE_UNDEFINED">
            <summary>                
                The const value use to indicate that
            <see cref="WebGpuSharp.TexelCopyBufferLayout.BytesPerRow">BytesPerRow</see> and <see cref="WebGpuSharp.TexelCopyBufferLayout.RowsPerImage">RowsPerImage</see>                
                is undefined.
            </summary>
        </comment>
        <comment location="DEPTH_CLEAR_VALUE_UNDEFINED">
            <summary>                
                The const value use to indicate that the
            <see cref="WebGpuSharp.FFI.RenderPassDepthStencilAttachmentFFI.DepthClearValue">DepthClearValue</see>                
                is undefined.
            </summary>
        </comment>
        <comment location="MIP_LEVEL_COUNT_UNDEFINED">
            <summary>                
                The const value use to indicate that the
            <see cref="WebGpuSharp.FFI.TextureViewDescriptorFFI.MipLevelCount">MipLevelCount</see>                
                is undefined.
            </summary>
        </comment>
        <comment location="DEPTH_SLICE_UNDEFINED">
            <summary>                
                The const value use to indicate that the
            <see cref="WebGpuSharp.FFI.RenderPassColorAttachmentFFI.DepthSlice">DepthSlice</see>                
                is undefined.
            </summary>
        </comment>
        <comment location="LIMIT_U32_UNDEFINED">
            <summary>                
                The const value use to indicate that a
            <see cref="uint"/> felid of <see cref="WebGpuSharp.Limits">Limits</see>                
                is undefined.
            </summary>
        </comment>
        <comment location="LIMIT_U64_UNDEFINED">
            <summary>                
                The const value use to indicate that a
            <see cref="ulong"/> felid of <see cref="WebGpuSharp.Limits">Limits</see>                
                is undefined.
            </summary>
        </comment>
        <comment location="QUERY_SET_INDEX_UNDEFINED">
            <summary>                
                The const value use to indicate that
            <see cref="WebGpuSharp.FFI.PassTimestampWritesFFI.BeginningOfPassWriteIndex">BeginningOfPassWriteIndex</see> and <see cref="WebGpuSharp.FFI.PassTimestampWritesFFI.EndOfPassWriteIndex">EndOfPassWriteIndex</see>                
                is undefined.
            </summary>
        </comment>
        <comment location="STRLEN">
            <summary>                
                A
            <see cref="WebGpuSharp.FFI.StringViewFFI">StringViewFFI</see> with its <see cref="WebGpuSharp.FFI.StringViewFFI.Length">Length</see>                
                as this value represent a null string for the webgpu FFI.
            </summary>
        </comment>
        <comment location="WHOLE_MAP_SIZE">
            <summary>                
                The const value use to indicate that the size for mapping should use whole rest of the buffer.
            </summary>
        </comment>
        <comment location="WHOLE_SIZE">
            <summary>                
                The const value use to indicate that the
            <see cref="WebGpuSharp.FFI.BindGroupEntryFFI.Size">BindGroupEntryFFI.Size</see>                
                is the whole buffer.
            </summary>
        </comment>
        <comment location="AdapterInfoFreeMembers">
            <summary>                
                Free members of a
            <see cref="WebGpuSharp.FFI.AdapterInfoFFI"/>                
                structure.
                After calling this function, using the members will lead to undefined behavior.
            </summary>
            <param name="adapterInfo">The <see cref="WebGpuSharp.FFI.AdapterInfoFFI"/> to free.</param>
        </comment>
        <comment location="CreateInstance">
            <summary>                
                Create a new instance of the WebGPU API. This is the first step in using the API.
                The instance is used to create adapters, which are used to create devices.
            </summary>
            <param name="descriptor">The options for the instance.</param>
        </comment>
        <comment location="SupportedFeaturesFreeMembers">
            <summary>                
